      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/DenizEmiraa/status/1974949362628231366",
      "text": "The Mariana Trench is 35,814 feet deep and is located in the western Pacific Ocean, east of the Philippines and south of Japan. \n\nIt's deepest point, the Challenger Deep, lies approximately 10,916 meters (35,814 feet) below sea level and is considered the deepest known place on Earth.\n\nThe trench is situated about 200 kilometers southwest of Guam, the nearest major island and part of the Mariana Islands. \n\nIt is approximately 2,500 kilometers from Manila, the capital of the Philippines. \n\nThe Mariana Trench was formed by the subduction of the Pacific Plate beneath the Mariana Plate and is part of the geologically active Ring of Fire. \n\nDue to its extreme depth and immense pressure, it remains one of the least explored places in the world. @grok ?",
